What's ISO 8583 & Message Flow - Part Two

Message Flow
This section specifies message flow for ATM and POS transactions. It shows how messages are exchanged and the routing and settlement impact associated with a given transaction. Each flow description includes a diagram showing which messages are exchanged between the acquirer, issuer, and switch.

1. Financial Transaction Message Flow
Financial transactions (01xx), (02xx), and (04xx) are used to process cash withdrawals, balance inquiries, purchases, adjustments, and cancellations. Except for balance inquiries, these transactions have a financial impact on cardholder accounts and result in the updating of system settlement totals.

A 0100/0200 message is a request to approve and post a financial transaction or to inquire about an account balance.

Message type codes are used to identify the general function of messages, and one Message type code is required in each message. The message types in the table are divided according to the ISO 8583 standard message classes. A Message Type Identifier (MTI) is a 4-digit numeric field that describes each message class & function. Some common MTIs are as below:

