1.1. Successful Transactions
Successful Transaction
(1, 2) Acquirer initiates a 0100/0200 message whenever it accepts another member’s card for processing. The message is a request for authorization of the transaction to the issuer. It is routed and logged through the network.
Network & through Issuer shall respond within a pre-set time with a 0110/0210 message to either authorize or decline the acquirer’s 0210/0110 request.

1.2. Network Time-Out on an Outstanding Financial Request
Network Time Out
Switch times out on an outstanding request to the issuer (0210 response is late or never received).

(1, 2) Acquirer initiates a 0100/0200 message whenever it accepts another member’s card for processing. The message is a request for authorization of the transaction to the issuer. It is routed and logged through the network.
(3, 4) in case the network times out on an outstanding request to the issuer, the switch shall generate a 0420 reversal advice message to the issuer to cancel the original 0100/0200 request.
(5) Network shall also respond to the acquirer with a 0110/0210 message which shall include response code 91 in field DE-39. This informs the acquirer that the issuer is inoperative.
(6) Switch shall expect a 0430 response from the issuer.
Note: Acquirer shall decline the transaction and advise the cardholder that the time out occurs on his transaction.

1.3. Acquirer Time-Out on an Outstanding Financial Request
Acquirer Time Out
The switch fails to respond to the acquirer within the pre-set time.

(1, 2) Acquirer initiates a 0100/0200 message whenever it accepts another member's card for processing. The message is a request for authorization of the transaction to the issuer. It is routed and logged through the network.
(3, 4,5, 6) In case the network fails to respond to the acquirer with a 0110/0210 message within the pre-set time, the acquirer shall initiate a 0420 reversal message to the issuer through the network, Network shall respond with a 0430 message (Reversal Response) to Acquirer.
(7, 8) if the response in 0110/0210 is approved then the network shall forward a 0420 reversal message to the issuer. The issuer shall respond with a 0430 message (Reversal Response) to the network. If the response in 0110/0210 is denied then the network shall not forward the 0420 reversal message to the issuer.
Note: Acquirer shall decline the transaction and advise the cardholder.

1.4. Reversal Transaction Flow
Reversal Transaction
The device fails to finish the transaction after the acquirer receives approval. This could be due to technical error, Acquirer failure to deliver the response to the cardholder leads to canceling the transaction.

(1, 2) Acquirer initiates a 0100/0200 message whenever it accepts another member’s card for processing. The message is a request for authorization of the transaction to the issuer. It is routed and logged through the network.
(3, 4) Issuer shall respond within a pre-set time with a 0110/0210 message to either authorize or decline the acquirer’s 0100/0200 request, network will forward the 0110/0210 to the acquirer.
(5, 6) in case the device fails to complete the process after the acquirer received Approval. The acquirer shall initiate a 420 reversal message to the network, switch shall respond with 0430 (reversal response) to the acquirer.
(7, 8) Network shall forward 0420 reversal messages to the issuer. The issuer shall respond with 0430 messages (Reversal Response) to the network.

